      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:09 a.m.\nAPPEARANCES:\nQUIN DENVIR, ESQ., Federal Defender, Sacramento, California; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nDONALD E. DE NICOLA, ESQ., Deputy Attorney General, Los Angeles, California; on behalf of the Respondent.\nMICHAEL CHERTOFF, ESQ., Assistant Attorney General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C., for United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Michael Chertoff",
      "case_id": "2002-01-6978",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64b94292e9cdf451c9b7f6881964c624f5f8b66c93a8ca6854fb0d6da152c48c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64b94292e9cd-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF MICHAEL CHERTOFF, ESQ.\nIn support of the Respondent"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-6978",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64b94292e9cdf451c9b7f6881964c624f5f8b66c93a8ca6854fb0d6da152c48c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64b94292e9cd-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: What was the value of the golf clubs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-6978",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64b94292e9cdf451c9b7f6881964c624f5f8b66c93a8ca6854fb0d6da152c48c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64b94292e9cd-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: It seems to me the question before us is, is it unreasonable to put away somebody who has this record?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Denvir",
      "case_id": "2002-01-6978",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64b94292e9cdf451c9b7f6881964c624f5f8b66c93a8ca6854fb0d6da152c48c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64b94292e9cd-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, first of all, as to the question of initiative versus legislation, it is my understanding that the Court, in other areas, has said that there's no greater deference given to one than the other. But the other question is, there's no doubt that some deference has to be paid by this Court to legislative judgments or initiative judgments in the questions of punishment and in dealing with recidivists."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-6978",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64b94292e9cdf451c9b7f6881964c624f5f8b66c93a8ca6854fb0d6da152c48c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64b94292e9cd-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: So how do you decide --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-01-6978",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64b94292e9cdf451c9b7f6881964c624f5f8b66c93a8ca6854fb0d6da152c48c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64b94292e9cd-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "California considered that when they set the penalties for grand theft. And they set the penalty as a maximum of three years in prison."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-01-6978",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64b94292e9cdf451c9b7f6881964c624f5f8b66c93a8ca6854fb0d6da152c48c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64b94292e9cd-0001-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the way the statute is written is that if the prior felonies meet the statutory definition of being serious or violent -- if you have two of those, then any new felony triggers the three-strike sentence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-6978",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64b94292e9cdf451c9b7f6881964c624f5f8b66c93a8ca6854fb0d6da152c48c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64b94292e9cd-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Possibly be constitutional or unconstitutional?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-6978",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64b94292e9cdf451c9b7f6881964c624f5f8b66c93a8ca6854fb0d6da152c48c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64b94292e9cd-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But serious or violent -- it really doesn't have to be violent; it has to serious. But you could have had $1200 thefts, four or five of them, and he would still qualify, wouldn't he?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. De Nicola",
      "case_id": "2002-01-6978",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64b94292e9cdf451c9b7f6881964c624f5f8b66c93a8ca6854fb0d6da152c48c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64b94292e9cd-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DE NICOLA: No, Your Honor. If -- the prior crimes have to qualify as serious or violent under the definitions of a separate statutory scheme, so they would not --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-6978",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64b94292e9cdf451c9b7f6881964c624f5f8b66c93a8ca6854fb0d6da152c48c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64b94292e9cd-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: On Justice Stevens' hypo, taking it one step further, I guess we would have to say that if there were 15 prior speeding offenses, and they had been classified as felonies in California, that there was no disproportion between 25-to-life for 15 -- with a predicate of 15 prior speeding offenses, on the one hand, and the penalties for torture and murder, on the other hand."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. De Nicola",
      "case_id": "2002-01-6978",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "64b94292e9cdf451c9b7f6881964c624f5f8b66c93a8ca6854fb0d6da152c48c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-64b94292e9cd-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DE NICOLA: Yes, we do adopt the theory of incapacitation, and we do rely on incapacitation as a theory"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
